        {
          "id": "f1",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Start and finish",
          "text": "A terminal marks start or end.\n\nA flow line shows the next step.\n\nEvery intended path needs a clear destination.\n\nChallenge: Why should an arrow have a clear direction?\n\nIt shows which instruction executes next."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Read and write",
          "text": "A parallelogram represents input or output.\n\nLabel the action and the data.\n\nInputs and outputs are different operations.\n\nChallenge: Which symbol should contain Input age?\n\nAn input/output parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "id": "f3",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Process the data",
          "text": "A rectangle represents a process.\n\nUse it for calculations or assignments.\n\nShow the operation clearly.\n\nChallenge: Which symbol should contain total = total + 3?\n\nA process rectangle, because the value is being updated."
        },
        {
          "id": "f4",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Branch on a decision",
          "text": "A diamond contains a condition.\n\nLabel outgoing paths Yes/No or True/False.\n\nBoth outcomes must be handled.\n\nChallenge: What is missing if only the Yes path is drawn?\n\nThe behaviour when the item is unavailable is not defined."
        },
        {
          "id": "f5",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Use a subprogram",
          "text": "A predefined-process symbol calls a named subprogram.\n\nIts detailed steps may be shown elsewhere.\n\nIt supports a clear top-level algorithm.\n\nChallenge: How does a subprogram symbol help a large flowchart?\n\nIt keeps the main diagram manageable while detailed steps are defined separately."
        },
        {
          "id": "f6",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Check every route",
          "text": "Trace each branch using sample data.\n\nCheck that arrows connect correctly.\n\nCompare outputs with the requirement.\n\nChallenge: Why test both branches?\n\nA correct true path does not prove the false path behaves correctly."
        }
      ],
